WEBVTT

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:41.854
Sis, is that you?

00:00:42.063 --> 00:00:44.190
> I'm home! )

00:00:47.944 --> 00:00:51.239
Feel free to come leap into my arms.

00:00:51.447 --> 00:00:53.157
I'll pass.

00:00:53.366 --> 00:00:56.828
Even though I'm home after being
away for so long? You're no fun.

00:00:57.036 --> 00:00:58.496
Hmph.

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:06.296
I scowled at the wind blowing
at my window of boredom

00:01:06.504 --> 00:01:14.804
so I could turn away
the awkwardness I was feeling

00:01:14.804 --> 00:01:14.929
"Hyouka" so I could turn away
the awkwardness I was feeling

00:01:14.929 --> 00:01:22.687
"Hyouka"

00:01:22.770 --> 00:01:28.026
I nod noncommittally at today
as I hold it in my hand

00:01:28.234 --> 00:01:33.406
projecting myself a little exaggeratedly

00:01:33.615 --> 00:01:38.786
I get the feeling that
something is about to change

00:01:38.995 --> 00:01:44.292
It's all because of you
calling out to my heart

00:01:45.501 --> 00:01:50.715
Peeking up at cloudy skies,
| sense what's coming

00:01:50.923 --> 00:01:59.140
Let's reach out our hands
with courage stronger than ever

00:01:59.349 --> 00:02:03.686
Light and shadow are both still far off

00:02:03.895 --> 00:02:10.026
but even so, we want to know
the reason for this kindness

00:02:10.234 --> 00:02:17.492
Let's go look now, beyond the brilliance
that goes by nobody's name

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:26.417
before it all becomes a thing of the past

00:02:33.132 --> 00:02:36.511
"What Should Be Had"

00:02:36.511 --> 00:02:37.512
"What Should Be Had"
Is this a South American souvenir?

00:02:37.512 --> 00:02:39.597
Is this a South American souvenir?

00:02:39.806 --> 00:02:42.350
Yes it is. You wanted one, right?

00:02:42.558 --> 00:02:44.268
Not really.

00:02:55.571 --> 00:02:56.781
Good morning.

00:02:56.989 --> 00:02:59.242
Let's now turn to the weather forecast

00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:00.493
--This is unusual--you, watching TV?
--around the country.

00:03:00.493 --> 00:03:02.787
--This is unusual--you, watching TV?
--First, cloud conditions around Japan.

00:03:02.787 --> 00:03:03.496
--What about the paper?
--First, cloud conditions around Japan.

00:03:03.705 --> 00:03:06.040
--I don't want to work my brain.
--There's a powerful high pressure zone from the Pacific

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:06.874
--Hmm...
--There's a powerful high pressure zone from the Pacific

00:03:06.874 --> 00:03:08.251
--Hmm...
--encompassing a broad area from the west to the east,

00:03:08.251 --> 00:03:10.420
--encompassing a broad area from the west to the east,

00:03:10.628 --> 00:03:12.422
with areas of clearing increasing.

00:03:12.630 --> 00:03:14.382
--You sure seem to have lots of free time.
--Here is the temperature forecast.

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:16.342
--My schedule is crammed full.
--Some parts will experience highs of over 33 degrees during the day,

00:03:16.342 --> 00:03:18.219
--Schedule? Doing what?
--Some parts will experience highs of over 33 degrees during the day,

00:03:18.428 --> 00:03:20.555
--Napping.
--with periods of intense lingering heat.

00:03:20.763 --> 00:03:23.599
--There's a job where you can make ¥500, --Those who
are susceptible to heat stroke should be extra careful.

00:03:23.808 --> 00:03:26.477
--Just by sitting there. How about it?
--Now for the precipitation forecast.

00:03:26.686 --> 00:03:27.603
--Mm.
--Clear skies will continue throughout the day,

00:03:27.603 --> 00:03:28.604
--Interested? Or not?
--Clear skies will continue throughout the day,

00:03:28.813 --> 00:03:30.898
-Mm.
--but moist air will be moving in from the Pacific,

00:03:31.107 --> 00:03:32.567
--Okay, that settles it!
--so there will be scattered showers and thunderstorms in the afternoon.

00:03:32.567 --> 00:03:36.195
--I'll let them know you're interested.
--so there will be scattered showers and thunderstorms in the afternoon.

00:03:36.404 --> 00:03:39.657
As we enter September,
the mornings will finally cool off,

00:03:39.866 --> 00:03:41.242
--and autumn is starting to make its presence felt,

00:03:41.242 --> 00:03:41.743
--Here.
--and autumn is starting to make its presence felt,

00:03:41.951 --> 00:03:46.080
--Use it when you get to work.
--but the intense summer heat will still continue during the day.

00:03:49.917 --> 00:03:53.171
Yes, Oreki residence. Ah, Satoshi-kun?

00:03:53.379 --> 00:03:54.756
It's been a long time.

00:03:54.964 --> 00:03:57.300
Yes, I just got back.

00:03:57.508 --> 00:04:01.471
Hotaro? Yeah, he's here. Just a moment, okay?

00:04:01.679 --> 00:04:04.891
Hotaro! Phone call from Satoshi-kun!

00:04:05.099 --> 00:04:06.768
Mm.

00:04:06.976 --> 00:04:10.646
Hotaro, have you finished reading
that book I lent you yet?

00:04:10.855 --> 00:04:11.773
Mm.

00:04:11.981 --> 00:04:15.026
If you're done reading it,
I'd like to get it back.

00:04:15.234 --> 00:04:16.319
Mm.

00:04:16.527 --> 00:04:18.696
Can I come pick it up today?

00:04:18.905 --> 00:04:22.825
Mm... After my job, yeah.

00:04:23.034 --> 00:04:23.493
Huh?

00:04:23.701 --> 00:04:25.787
After my job.

00:04:25.995 --> 00:04:30.374
A job?! You, Hotaro?! What on
Earth has come over you?!

00:04:30.583 --> 00:04:33.795
Oh, you know. I'm pinch-hitting
for someone Sis knows,

00:04:34.003 --> 00:04:35.588
being a lifeguard at the municipal pool.

00:04:35.797 --> 00:04:38.883
Huh, your sister, eh? Say no more.

00:04:39.091 --> 00:04:41.594
Imagine, you, earning by
the sweat of your brow.

00:04:41.803 --> 00:04:43.638
| have to go now, so I'm hanging up.

00:04:43.846 --> 00:04:46.599
All right. I'll come by to cool off later.

00:04:46.808 --> 00:04:48.726
Suit yourself. Bye.

00:04:48.935 --> 00:04:50.186
Bye.

00:05:18.464 --> 00:05:20.383
Hotaro!

00:05:20.591 --> 00:05:22.301
Hey! We're here.

00:05:28.015 --> 00:05:30.726
| wasn't expecting all three of you.

00:05:30.935 --> 00:05:33.354
| reached out to the other two
after I hung up with you.

00:05:33.563 --> 00:05:36.023
| told them we were in for an
extremely exceptional sight.

00:05:36.232 --> 00:05:38.150
Fuku-chan, is this it?

00:05:38.359 --> 00:05:39.151
Yep.

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:41.821
"The Hotaro at work."

00:05:42.029 --> 00:05:44.115
Honestly, I'm a bit disappointed.

00:05:44.323 --> 00:05:46.492
Now, now, as long as we're here,

00:05:46.701 --> 00:05:48.744
let's all enjoy ourselves together.

00:05:48.953 --> 00:05:52.874
Yeah, you're right. As long as we're here.

00:05:53.958 --> 00:05:55.376
Hey, you!

00:05:56.460 --> 00:05:58.921
Stop eyeballing my woman, you creep!

00:05:59.130 --> 00:06:00.590
Come on, stop it.

00:06:00.798 --> 00:06:02.174
No, I wasn't...

00:06:02.383 --> 00:06:05.177
Sir, please, take it easy.

00:06:05.386 --> 00:06:07.138
What's that about?

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:11.267
Please, let me not get involved...

00:06:11.475 --> 00:06:14.228
--Come on, you can do it.
--Here it comes!

00:06:19.066 --> 00:06:21.027
Okay, here it comes!

00:06:21.235 --> 00:06:22.904
Off you go!

00:06:25.156 --> 00:06:26.198
Here!

00:06:27.283 --> 00:06:28.326
Ha!

00:06:29.285 --> 00:06:30.286
Bump.

00:06:31.454 --> 00:06:32.955
Chitanda-san! "Sepak takraw" it!

00:06:33.164 --> 00:06:35.207
Huh? Sep--

00:06:37.585 --> 00:06:39.003
You're hopeless, Chi-chan.

00:06:39.211 --> 00:06:42.798
Okay, Chitanda-san plays the penalty game!

00:07:00.232 --> 00:07:02.151
I"'m S o r ry 1 Il m S o rry I

00:07:08.908 --> 00:07:10.785
Here we go!

00:07:11.744 --> 00:07:12.995
Ready, set...

00:07:13.204 --> 00:07:14.580
Go!

00:07:18.918 --> 00:07:20.586
Here I go!

00:07:20.795 --> 00:07:23.756
Away!

00:07:32.556 --> 00:07:34.183
Hey!

00:07:34.392 --> 00:07:37.061
Time to switch. You can take a break.

00:07:45.027 --> 00:07:46.821
Oreki-san...

00:07:47.029 --> 00:07:49.699
Would you like to have some lunch together?

00:07:51.075 --> 00:07:53.285
If you would have told me a little sooner,

00:07:53.494 --> 00:07:56.455
| could have prepared
something better for lunch.

00:07:56.664 --> 00:07:59.041
| wish you would tell Hotaro that.

00:07:59.250 --> 00:08:00.251
Why is that?

00:08:00.459 --> 00:08:04.505
Well, this is Hotaro, the walking,
talking, monument to idleness.

00:08:04.714 --> 00:08:07.591
And suddenly, his working spirit comes to life.

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:09.510
There's no way we could pass this up.

00:08:09.719 --> 00:08:11.178
Right, Hotaro?

00:08:11.387 --> 00:08:12.930
Mm.

00:08:16.183 --> 00:08:20.563
Still, it's so much fun for us
to all get together like this.

00:08:20.771 --> 00:08:22.982
Oh, yeah...

00:08:23.190 --> 00:08:25.526
| have to say, it's not a good match.

00:08:25.735 --> 00:08:27.361
What's that?

00:08:28.654 --> 00:08:31.073
The pool and Hotaro.

00:08:31.282 --> 00:08:32.241
That's for sure.

00:08:32.450 --> 00:08:34.243
You two are being awful.

00:08:34.452 --> 00:08:36.871
Swimsuits and Oreki don't go together, either.

00:08:37.079 --> 00:08:40.374
Mm-hm! The sun and Hotaro, either.

00:08:40.583 --> 00:08:41.667
The sea and Oreki!

00:08:41.876 --> 00:08:43.335
Summer and Hotaro!

00:08:43.544 --> 00:08:46.922
Come on, that's enough, already.
Right, Oreki-san?

00:08:47.131 --> 00:08:48.632
Mm.

00:08:50.217 --> 00:08:53.054
Well, how about we get back to the pool?

00:08:53.262 --> 00:08:56.390
Yeah. Well, I'll clean up our trash.

00:08:56.599 --> 00:09:00.352
Okay then, I'll put our chairs back.

00:09:00.561 --> 00:09:02.396
There we go.

00:09:09.445 --> 00:09:12.281
Huh? You still want more?

00:09:12.490 --> 00:09:15.618
What am I going to do with you?

00:09:15.826 --> 00:09:18.829
Well, let's go buy another one.

00:09:20.623 --> 00:09:22.458
That was startling, huh?

00:09:22.666 --> 00:09:24.043
Yeah.

00:09:27.588 --> 00:09:29.548
How is the job?

00:09:29.757 --> 00:09:32.384
Mm, about average.

00:09:32.593 --> 00:09:35.554
I'd like to try it once, myself.

00:09:35.763 --> 00:09:36.889
Mm.

00:09:46.398 --> 00:09:48.109
Aren't they fast!

00:09:50.444 --> 00:09:50.986
Mm.

00:09:51.195 --> 00:09:54.824
| wonder if their dream is to grow up
to be competitive swimmers.

00:09:55.032 --> 00:09:56.283
Mm.

00:09:56.492 --> 00:10:02.289
One of them might end up
winning a gold medal, huh?

00:10:02.498 --> 00:10:03.624
Who knows?

00:10:03.833 --> 00:10:04.542
Huh?

00:10:04.750 --> 00:10:08.212
It all depends on whether or not
they're that kind of person.

00:10:08.420 --> 00:10:14.051
If they're someone special, they will;
if they're normal, they won't.

00:10:15.886 --> 00:10:20.266
Oreki-san, would you like to be special?

00:10:20.474 --> 00:10:24.728
Not really. Whatever I do,
I'll be a normal person.

00:10:28.649 --> 00:10:32.069
Oreki-san, you are special! To me, anyway!

00:10:32.278 --> 00:10:32.862
Huh?

00:10:33.070 --> 00:10:35.447
Fukube-san and Mayaka-san are also special.

00:10:35.656 --> 00:10:40.995
Everyone with whom I am
involved is special to me.

00:10:41.203 --> 00:10:44.665
Nevermind your subjective views.
Generally speaking, I--

00:10:44.874 --> 00:10:46.667
Doesn't subjectivity count?

00:10:46.876 --> 00:10:47.918
Compared to those around us,

00:10:48.127 --> 00:10:52.339
we don't have to be concerned with
"normal" or "special," do we?

00:10:52.548 --> 00:10:56.135
As long as there's someone, even just
one person, who thinks you're special,

00:10:56.343 --> 00:10:59.513
then I think that's good enough.

00:10:59.722 --> 00:11:03.434
Oh, I mean, um...

00:11:03.642 --> 00:11:05.477
Excuse me!

00:11:10.024 --> 00:11:12.318
"Hakuro ('Bright Dews')" "For gray skies at length
gather, and morning dews are full and hoary"

00:11:12.318 --> 00:11:13.027
"Hyouka™ “"Hakuro ('Bright Dews")" "For gray skies at
length gather, and morning dews are full and hoary"

00:11:14.528 --> 00:11:16.238
Wait up!

00:11:18.991 --> 00:11:21.452
Oreki-san, you are special!

00:11:22.578 --> 00:11:24.455
Doesn't subjectivity count?

00:11:37.927 --> 00:11:41.805
Oreki-kun, time to switch.
Go take a break.

00:11:55.861 --> 00:11:57.738
Um, Oreki-san...

00:11:57.947 --> 00:11:59.448
Mm.

00:11:59.657 --> 00:12:04.036
Um... There's something I'm curious about.

00:12:04.245 --> 00:12:04.995
Huh?

00:12:05.204 --> 00:12:08.415
It falls within the category of your job.

00:12:08.624 --> 00:12:11.961
You know that woman over
there in the red swimsuit?

00:12:12.169 --> 00:12:13.796
Mm.

00:12:14.004 --> 00:12:17.174
When we were finishing our lunch,

00:12:17.383 --> 00:12:20.219
she had something white on her left ear.

00:12:20.427 --> 00:12:23.889
But looking at her now, it's not there.

00:12:24.098 --> 00:12:26.433
I'm surprised you noticed
something like that.

00:12:26.642 --> 00:12:30.354
Oh, no, I really just happened
to notice it by accident.

00:12:31.772 --> 00:12:33.941
So? What about it?

00:12:34.149 --> 00:12:39.071
Don't "what about it" us! What if that
were an earring, or a piercing?

00:12:39.280 --> 00:12:43.409
If someone happens to step on it,
they could end up being hurt.

00:12:49.456 --> 00:12:53.002
Oreki-san, would you come
look for it with us?

00:12:53.794 --> 00:12:57.506
Some place as big as this is? Is she serious?

00:12:59.300 --> 00:13:01.635
Are you sure she had it on her ear?

00:13:01.844 --> 00:13:02.553
Yes.

00:13:02.761 --> 00:13:06.849
Then before you go looking for it,
you should check with her, first.

00:13:07.057 --> 00:13:09.643
| would like to do that, but...

00:13:12.021 --> 00:13:13.939
It's kind of hard to ask her.

00:13:14.148 --> 00:13:17.776
It's not like you're asking her
something out of place. You'll be fine.

00:13:17.985 --> 00:13:20.904
Then you go and ask her.

00:13:21.113 --> 00:13:22.114
I'll pass.

00:13:22.323 --> 00:13:23.073
Hmph.

00:13:23.282 --> 00:13:25.117
Please, Oreki-san?

00:13:25.326 --> 00:13:27.453
Oreki, you're a lifeguard, right?

00:13:27.661 --> 00:13:29.330
What do you say, Hotaro?

00:13:32.833 --> 00:13:35.085
| am curious!

00:13:45.888 --> 00:13:46.680
Huh?

00:13:46.889 --> 00:13:48.891
The one with the guy who got angry?

00:13:49.099 --> 00:13:51.268
This is turning into a real problem.

00:13:51.477 --> 00:13:52.394
Yeah.

00:13:52.603 --> 00:13:55.272
Oreki-kun, I don't want this
to become a big deal,

00:13:55.481 --> 00:13:57.107
so start looking for it discreetly.

00:13:57.316 --> 00:14:00.027
Okay, but I can't do it alone.

00:14:00.235 --> 00:14:03.238
Mm-hm, well, there are other
lifeguards around there;

00:14:03.447 --> 00:14:05.574
I'll have them check around the poolside.

00:14:05.783 --> 00:14:08.285
Oreki-kun, you take inside the pool.

00:14:08.494 --> 00:14:09.536
Okay.

00:14:09.745 --> 00:14:11.080
| will help you.

00:14:11.288 --> 00:14:12.373
So will |, of course.

00:14:12.581 --> 00:14:14.249
Well, what choice do I have?

00:14:14.458 --> 00:14:15.542
Thanks.

00:14:15.751 --> 00:14:18.712
Okay then, how are we going to look for it?

00:14:18.921 --> 00:14:21.298
We should probably split the place up.

00:14:21.507 --> 00:14:24.635
Yes. What do you think, Oreki-san?

00:14:24.843 --> 00:14:25.677
Knock yourselves out.

00:14:25.886 --> 00:14:28.764
Look, you! Show a little motivation!

00:14:28.972 --> 00:14:32.226
Quite right. You really are
being a goldbricker.

00:14:32.434 --> 00:14:35.062
Would you at least divvy up our areas?

00:14:37.398 --> 00:14:41.068
All right. I'll come up
with them. Let's see...

00:14:41.276 --> 00:14:44.029
Chitanda-san and Mayaka
will take the stair area;

00:14:44.238 --> 00:14:46.198
Hotaro will take the slide area;

00:14:46.407 --> 00:14:48.367
I'll take the diving board area.

00:14:48.575 --> 00:14:49.868
How does that sound?

00:14:50.077 --> 00:14:50.953
All right!

00:14:51.161 --> 00:14:52.079
Sure, why not?

00:14:52.287 --> 00:14:53.288
Go ahead.

00:14:57.459 --> 00:14:58.168
Hotaro...

00:14:58.377 --> 00:14:59.128
Hm?

00:14:59.336 --> 00:15:03.048
Is this job something you "have to do"?

00:15:05.551 --> 00:15:06.510
I'm not sure.

00:15:06.718 --> 00:15:09.096
What, you never thought about it?

00:15:09.304 --> 00:15:12.099
Kind of a sorry excuse
for a motto, isn't it?

00:15:12.307 --> 00:15:13.559
Well, excuse me.

00:15:13.767 --> 00:15:15.853
Yeah, there it is.

00:15:16.061 --> 00:15:21.442
At least give some reaction, even if
it is griping. You're being a bore.

00:15:21.650 --> 00:15:24.027
Bye now. I'll see you later.

00:16:20.125 --> 00:16:21.293
Oreki!

00:16:23.462 --> 00:16:26.381
Don't just stand there.

00:16:26.590 --> 00:16:31.053
I'm not. I picked up a tiddlywink,
and I was just throwing it away.

00:16:31.261 --> 00:16:32.679
Yeah, I'll bet.

00:16:39.394 --> 00:16:45.943
Oreki, looking at you now just
drains me. Frankly, it's a pain.

00:16:46.151 --> 00:16:47.569
So don't look at me.

00:16:47.778 --> 00:16:53.450
When I looked at you before,
it annoyed me. That was a pain, too.

00:16:54.493 --> 00:16:56.828
Either way, you're going to be a pain.

00:16:57.037 --> 00:17:00.832
So would you at least go back
to the way you were before?

00:17:02.668 --> 00:17:05.963
| liked you better when you
were at least responsive.

00:17:10.008 --> 00:17:12.469
Liked me better, huh?

00:17:29.778 --> 00:17:31.029
Hm...

00:17:33.699 --> 00:17:34.700
Did you find it?

00:17:34.908 --> 00:17:38.036
No. But we might not have to look anymore.

00:17:38.245 --> 00:17:43.041
Ah! Which means that you've
figured something out, right?

00:17:49.756 --> 00:17:51.967
Mm-mm, it's all right.

00:17:52.175 --> 00:17:53.176
Chitanda,

00:17:53.385 --> 00:17:56.430
are you sure it was an
earring that you saw?

00:17:56.638 --> 00:17:59.224
| can't say for sure. It's just,

00:17:59.433 --> 00:18:03.520
I'm sure that there was
something white on her left ear.

00:18:03.729 --> 00:18:07.274
If it was just on one side,
it could have been a piercing.

00:18:07.482 --> 00:18:10.819
No, I'm not asking what
kind of jewelry it was.

00:18:11.028 --> 00:18:14.239
I'm asking whether it was actually
jewelry in the first place.

00:18:14.448 --> 00:18:16.617
Huh? What do you mean?

00:18:16.825 --> 00:18:18.368
Look over there.

00:18:18.577 --> 00:18:21.496
If she was wearing anything in her ear,

00:18:21.705 --> 00:18:24.625
she wouldn't be smacking her
ears so blithely, would she?

00:18:24.833 --> 00:18:26.293
Meaning?

00:18:26.501 --> 00:18:28.211
Whatever she had on her ear

00:18:28.420 --> 00:18:31.381
was probably something that got there
without her even knowing it.

00:18:31.590 --> 00:18:34.468
If that's true, what are you saying it was?

00:18:34.676 --> 00:18:36.219
That's the question.

00:18:36.428 --> 00:18:39.389
Satoshi, would you scoop up Ibara for me?

00:18:39.598 --> 00:18:40.849
Okay.

00:18:46.188 --> 00:18:49.232
Wait! Out here in the open?!

00:18:49.441 --> 00:18:51.193
Okay, what if Chitanda did it?

00:18:51.401 --> 00:18:53.278
Having Chi-chan do it
doesn't make it any better!

00:18:53.487 --> 00:18:56.948
I'll look like a little kid,
and that's embarrassing, you know!

00:18:57.157 --> 00:19:01.286
Well, seeing what a little kid
would do is what I'm checking for.

00:19:01.495 --> 00:19:04.081
Why would you want me to do that, anyway?

00:19:04.289 --> 00:19:05.832
I'm proving a theory.

00:19:06.041 --> 00:19:07.668
A theory about this matter?

00:19:07.876 --> 00:19:09.211
Yeah.

00:19:16.259 --> 00:19:18.679
| don't mind at all.

00:19:24.184 --> 00:19:27.312
All right, fine! I'll do it, then.

00:19:33.235 --> 00:19:35.529
Chitanda-san, you're pretty strong, huh?

00:19:35.737 --> 00:19:36.655
What does that mean?!

00:19:36.863 --> 00:19:39.658
Oh, nothing! I didn't mean it that way.

00:19:39.866 --> 00:19:42.536
| was just offering a general observation.

00:19:42.744 --> 00:19:44.413
Hm, sure enough.

00:19:44.621 --> 00:19:46.540
Sure enough, what?

00:19:46.748 --> 00:19:49.626
Her hand. Normally, she'd
put it on your shoulder.

00:19:49.835 --> 00:19:52.129
Say, can I get down now?

00:19:52.337 --> 00:19:54.631
Yeah, that's fine.

00:19:54.840 --> 00:19:57.092
Down you go.

00:19:58.218 --> 00:19:59.928
Take a look over there.

00:20:00.887 --> 00:20:05.308
Earlier, I saw that woman
holding that child.

00:20:05.517 --> 00:20:07.936
She's probably his mother, or something.

00:20:08.145 --> 00:20:12.566
If he was holding that ice cream at
the time, what would have happened?

00:20:12.774 --> 00:20:17.279
That's it! The ice cream would be
right where it could touch her ear!

00:20:17.487 --> 00:20:19.197
And there you have it.

00:20:20.866 --> 00:20:23.285
Then, the reason it isn't there now is...

00:20:23.493 --> 00:20:25.328
It either came off when she was swimming,

00:20:25.537 --> 00:20:27.581
or someone told her it was there.

00:20:27.789 --> 00:20:29.624
That would explain it.

00:20:32.085 --> 00:20:35.172
U-Um, Oreki-san...

00:20:35.380 --> 00:20:36.298
What is it?

00:20:36.506 --> 00:20:39.092
Um... that is...

00:20:39.301 --> 00:20:44.431
Oreki-san, this is something that |
really think is amazing about you!

00:20:49.352 --> 00:20:50.187
Hmph.

00:20:50.395 --> 00:20:52.564
Flattery will get you nowhere!

00:20:57.569 --> 00:20:58.820
Right.

00:20:59.029 --> 00:21:02.616
It's been a long time since
we've seen Hotaro cracking wise.

00:21:02.824 --> 00:21:03.909
Something wrong with that?

00:21:04.117 --> 00:21:08.038
Yes, there is. Without it,
it puts us off our stride.

00:21:08.246 --> 00:21:09.164
Hmph.

00:21:10.749 --> 00:21:15.045
Oh, I forgot. I haven't yet thanked you.

00:21:16.129 --> 00:21:19.257
Oreki-san, thank you very much.

00:21:19.466 --> 00:21:22.260
I'm sorry for causing all this fuss.

00:21:22.469 --> 00:21:23.762
No, that's okay.

00:21:23.970 --> 00:21:25.472
Chi-chan, you don't have to.

00:21:25.680 --> 00:21:28.517
I'm the one who said it was
an earring or piercing.

00:21:28.725 --> 00:21:30.393
Oreki, I'm sorry.

00:21:30.602 --> 00:21:32.062
It's okay, just stop.

00:21:32.270 --> 00:21:37.776
Well, after this little break,
I'm starting to get hungry.

00:21:37.984 --> 00:21:40.153
Maybe I'll have some ice cream--

00:21:40.362 --> 00:21:42.739
What about the ice cream?

00:21:42.948 --> 00:21:44.866
Ah! Hyoukal!

00:21:45.075 --> 00:21:50.038
Fuku-chan, you said that this time, you would turn in
your Hyouka draft to me tomorrow, rain or shine!

00:21:50.247 --> 00:21:52.123
Well? Is it done yet?

00:21:52.332 --> 00:21:56.169
W-Well, it's more-or-less done,
| guess you could say.

00:21:56.378 --> 00:21:59.422
Which means it's not done,
right? Isn't that so?!

00:21:59.631 --> 00:22:01.341
I-I guess you could say that, too.

00:22:01.550 --> 00:22:03.635
You can't say it's anything else!

00:22:03.844 --> 00:22:04.970
Come on, Fuku-chan!

00:22:05.178 --> 00:22:07.514
We're going home right now,
and you're writing your draft!

00:22:07.722 --> 00:22:11.226
I'm not letting you out of my sight
the rest of the day until you finish it!

00:22:11.434 --> 00:22:15.480
L-Look, I just have a little bit more
to do, so I can do it myself.

00:22:15.689 --> 00:22:17.732
|I don't believe you!

00:22:17.941 --> 00:22:22.195
Oh, Chi-chan, Oreki, sorry.
We're heading out. See you tomorrow.

00:22:22.404 --> 00:22:23.697
Goodbye--

00:22:25.782 --> 00:22:27.993
| hope they get that draft finished.

00:22:28.201 --> 00:22:32.414
| don't know. I mean,
the thrill is all in the chase.

00:22:32.622 --> 00:22:34.749
They should just get to it, already.

00:22:34.958 --> 00:22:36.835
In the chase...?

00:22:37.043 --> 00:22:40.589
| went and turned again
to you for help today.

00:22:40.797 --> 00:22:42.299
Sorry to always do that.

00:22:42.507 --> 00:22:44.759
Damn right. You're such a nuisance.

00:22:44.968 --> 00:22:47.012
Ah! That's not nice.

00:22:48.763 --> 00:22:50.056
On the other hand,

00:22:50.265 --> 00:22:52.517
maybe that's not a bad thing.

00:22:52.726 --> 00:22:53.435
Hm?

00:22:53.643 --> 00:22:55.896
Nothing, never mind.

00:22:58.648 --> 00:23:00.859
Ah! Come to think of it, Oreki-san,

00:23:01.067 --> 00:23:04.613
how did you know the
white stuff was ice cream?

00:23:04.821 --> 00:23:05.989
Oh, that?

00:23:06.197 --> 00:23:10.285
It's simple. There's nothing
else here that is white.

00:23:13.079 --> 00:23:15.498
| guess there is one other thing...

00:23:15.707 --> 00:23:17.042
Huh?

00:23:24.925 --> 00:23:27.218
W-Well, I should get going, too.

00:23:27.427 --> 00:23:29.679
Good luck with your work.

00:23:29.888 --> 00:23:31.598
Y-Yeah.

00:23:40.899 --> 00:23:42.067
Hey!

00:23:43.443 --> 00:23:45.195
Time to switch.

00:23:45.403 --> 00:23:46.947
Right.

00:23:54.537 --> 00:23:56.164
What a pain.

00:24:05.048 --> 00:24:07.801
Tonight it turns to love

00:24:08.009 --> 00:24:11.554
Meet me in a pleasant dream

00:24:11.763 --> 00:24:15.558
Make sure that you find me, okay?

00:24:15.767 --> 00:24:21.106
Our snooze-time date

00:24:33.326 --> 00:24:42.210
The heat of your budding warmth troubles me

00:24:44.087 --> 00:24:53.263
Don't you understand how I feel yet?

00:24:53.471 --> 00:24:58.768
There isn't supposed to be
any significance in your glance

00:24:58.977 --> 00:25:04.190
I mean, it's the same one
you give all your friends

00:25:04.399 --> 00:25:09.904
The tiny wishing star fading
into the morning light

00:25:10.113 --> 00:25:14.909
and the magic it works during the night
(I wish you would notice)

00:25:15.118 --> 00:25:17.871
Tonight it turns to love

00:25:18.079 --> 00:25:21.624
Meet me in a pleasant dream

00:25:21.833 --> 00:25:25.670
Make sure that you find me, okay?

00:25:25.879 --> 00:25:31.134
Our snooze-time date
